# VibeFW SPA Frontend

Vue 3 + TypeScript + Vite single-page application scaffolded by `php fw make:spa`.

## Tech Stack

| Package | Version | Purpose |
|---------|---------|---------|
| Vue 3 | ^3.x | Reactive UI framework |
| Vue Router | ^5.x | Client-side routing with auth guards |
| Pinia | ^3.x | Global state management |
| Vite | ^7.x | Dev server and build tool |
| TypeScript | ^5.x | Type safety |
| Axios | ^1.x | HTTP client for API calls |
| @velkymx/vibeui | latest | Bootstrap 5 component library |
| Vitest | latest | Unit testing |
| Playwright | latest | End-to-end testing |

## Quick Start

```bash
# Install dependencies (already done by make:spa)
npm install

# Start the dev server (hot-reload on http://localhost:5173)
npm run dev

# Build for production (outputs to ../public/spa/)
npm run build

# Run unit tests
npx vitest run

# Run e2e tests (requires the PHP backend to be running)
npx playwright test
```

## Project Structure

```
frontend/
├── src/
│   ├── main.ts                 # App entry — plugins, axios interceptor
│   ├── App.vue                 # Root component, global styles
│   ├── router/
│   │   └── index.ts            # Routes + auth navigation guards
│   ├── layouts/
│   │   └── MainLayout.vue      # Authenticated shell (sidebar + topbar)
│   ├── views/
│   │   ├── Home.vue            # Public landing page
│   │   ├── Dashboard.vue       # Protected dashboard (stats)
│   │   ├── auth/
│   │   │   ├── Login.vue       # Login form
│   │   │   └── Register.vue    # Registration form
│   │   └── errors/
│   │       └── NotFound.vue    # 404 catch-all
│   ├── types/
│   │   └── api.ts              # TypeScript interfaces for API responses
│   └── tests/
│       └── Dashboard.test.ts   # Example unit test
├── e2e/
│   └── example.spec.ts         # Example Playwright test
├── index.html                  # HTML entry point
├── vite.config.ts              # Vite configuration
├── tsconfig.json               # TypeScript configuration
└── package.json                # Dependencies and scripts
```

## Authentication Flow

1. **Login/Register** → POST to `/api/auth/login` or `/api/auth/register`
2. **Token storage** → Bearer token saved to `localStorage` under key `"token"`
3. **API requests** → Include `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header
4. **Route guards** → `router/index.ts` checks for token presence:
   - `meta: { auth: true }` → redirects to `/login` if no token
   - `meta: { guest: true }` → redirects to `/dashboard` if token exists
5. **Token expiration** → Global axios interceptor in `main.ts` catches 401 responses, clears the token, and redirects to `/login`

## API Endpoints

These endpoints are created by `make:spa` in your PHP backend:

| Method | Endpoint | Auth | Description |
|--------|----------|------|-------------|
| POST | `/api/auth/login` | No | Authenticate and receive token |
| POST | `/api/auth/register` | No | Create account and receive token |
| POST | `/api/auth/logout` | Yes | Invalidate token |
| GET | `/api/user` | Yes | Get authenticated user |
| GET | `/api/dashboard/stats` | Yes | Dashboard statistics (users, uptime, perf) |

### Validation Errors (422)

All endpoints return validation errors in this format:

```json
{
  "message": "Validation failed",
  "errors": {
    "email": "The email field is required.",
    "password": "The password must be at least 8 characters."
  }
}
```

Map these to VibeUI form components:

```vue
<VibeFormInput
  v-model="form.email"
  :validation-state="errors.email ? 'invalid' : null"
  :validation-message="errors.email"
/>
```

## VibeUI Components

All VibeUI components are registered globally — **no imports needed**.

```vue
<!-- Just use them in any template -->
<VibeButton variant="primary" :loading="saving">Save</VibeButton>
<VibeCard title="My Card"><template #body>Content</template></VibeCard>
<VibeIcon icon="house" size="2x" />
<VibeFormInput v-model="name" label="Name" />
<VibeAlert v-model="show" variant="success" message="Done!" />
```

**Important:** `validators` and `useFormValidation` must be imported:
```ts
import { validators, useFormValidation } from '@velkymx/vibeui'
```

Full component docs: https://github.com/velkymx/vibeui/blob/main/docs/README.md

## Dark Mode

Dark mode is handled automatically by Bootstrap 5.3. The toggle in `MainLayout.vue` sets `data-bs-theme="dark"` on the `<html>` element. Use Bootstrap CSS variables for colors:

```css
/* DO: uses CSS variables — adapts to dark mode */
color: var(--bs-body-color);
background-color: var(--bs-body-bg);

/* DON'T: hardcoded colors break in dark mode */
color: #212529;
background-color: #ffffff;
```

## Adding New Pages

1. Create `src/views/MyPage.vue`
2. Add a route in `src/router/index.ts` as a child of the MainLayout route:
   ```ts
   children: [
     { path: 'dashboard', name: 'dashboard', component: Dashboard },
     { path: 'my-page', name: 'my-page', component: MyPage },  // ← add here
   ]
   ```
3. Add a sidebar link in `src/layouts/MainLayout.vue`:
   ```vue
   <router-link to="/my-page" class="nav-link py-2 px-3 rounded mb-1" active-class="active">
     <VibeIcon icon="file-text" custom-class="me-2" /> My Page
   </router-link>
   ```

## Running the Full Stack

```bash
# Terminal 1: PHP backend
php fw serve

# Terminal 2: Vite dev server (proxies API calls to PHP)
cd frontend && npm run dev
```

For production, `npm run build` outputs to `public/spa/` which is served by PHP directly.
